<%# The reach-cap128 sweep's pre-registered reading (docs/design_record.md, 2026-10-01):
    `reading` is a Lab::ReachCap128Reading::Report. The per-run rows stay in
    `lab:reach_cap128_report`. %>
<% comparison = reading.comparison %>
<section class="mt-6" id="reach-cap128-reading">
  <h2>
    The pre-registered reading
    <span class="badge <%= reading.interim? ? 'badge-warning' : 'badge-success' %>">
      <%= reading.interim? ? "interim" : "final" %>
    </span>
  </h2>
  <p class="text-sm text-muted">
    <% if reading.interim? %>
      Interim: not every run of the two arms has finished and had every world it kept read by
      the readings pass, and only those that have are counted. Nothing here is the sweep's
      result yet.
    <% else %>
      Every run of the two arms has finished and had every world it kept read.
    <% end %>
    A run emerged where it has a confirmed emergence epoch and the orientation-aware census of
    some world it kept, from that epoch on, reads <span class="mono">replicator_share</span> of at
    least <%= percent_value Lab::ReachCap128Reading::MIN_SHARE %>. The control is the host–parasite
    sweep's economy-off arm at cap 128, at radius 1.
  </p>

  <figure class="table-figure mt-4">
    <figcaption class="table-caption text-sm text-muted" id="reach-cap128-arms">
      Runs per arm, counted so far. The rate is emerged over counted; the medians are over the
      emerged runs.
    </figcaption>
    <div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-labelledby="reach-cap128-arms">
      <table class="data-table" aria-labelledby="reach-cap128-arms">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Arm</th>
            <th class="numeric">Runs</th>
            <th class="numeric">Finished</th>
            <th class="numeric">Counted</th>
            <th class="numeric">Emerged</th>
            <th class="numeric">Rate</th>
            <th class="numeric">Median emergence epoch</th>
            <th class="numeric">Median terminal share</th>
            <th class="numeric">Median dominant length</th>
            <th class="numeric">Median dominant instructions</th>
            <th class="numeric">Eligible parents</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <% reading.arms.each do |arm| %>
            <tr>
              <td><%= arm.label %></td>
              <td class="numeric"><%= arm.rows.size %></td>
              <td class="numeric"><%= arm.finished %></td>
              <td class="numeric"><%= arm.counted %></td>
              <td class="numeric"><%= arm.emerged %></td>
              <td class="numeric"><%= percent_value arm.rate&.to_f %></td>
              <td class="numeric"><%= arm.median_emergence_epoch || "—" %></td>
              <td class="numeric"><%= percent_value arm.median_terminal_share %></td>
              <td class="numeric"><%= metric_value arm.median_raw_len %></td>
              <td class="numeric"><%= metric_value arm.median_instruction_count %></td>
              <td class="numeric"><%= arm.eligible_parents %></td>
            </tr>
          <% end %>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </figure>

  <h3 class="mt-4">H-reach128</h3>
  <p>
    Radius <%= Lab::ReachCap128Reading::TREATMENT_RADIUS %> with room to grow emerges more often than
    the cap-128 control at radius 1:
    <span class="badge <%= comparison.badge_class %>"><%= comparison.outcome_label %></span>
  </p>
  <p class="text-sm text-muted">
    <% if comparison.testable? %>
      One one-sided Fisher exact test at p &lt; <%= Lab::ReachCap128Reading::LEVEL %>:
      <%= comparison.counts %>, p = <%= metric_value comparison.p_value.to_f %>.
    <% else %>
      Untested until both arms have a counted run.
    <% end %>
    An eligible parent is an emerged world whose terminal stored world reads a share of at least
    <%= percent_value Lab::ReachCap128Reading::PARENT_SHARE %>; no later sweep's parent rule is
    set by it.
  </p>
</section>
